<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- The Thrift Chrome (WO32): an ordinary Google Chrome with its own profile (~/thrift/chrome-cross), next to the owner's
     own Chrome and the Poshmark poster's profile. The Thrift crosslister extension (ext/) runs in it, loaded unpacked
     once by hand. No remote debugging, no automation flags, no load-extension: the sites see a person's Chrome.
     WO54 §4 (live 2026-11-09: open since 1 AM with old pages restored — hers on eBay, Vinted with ad frames — 9.6 GB on
     her 8 GB laptop, two pages burning a core each): it is not her browser and runs only while there is work.
     - RunAtLoad false and no KeepAlive: launchd never starts it by itself (not at login, not after it quits). The poster
       starts it when its extension has a job (services.sh start chrome → launchctl kickstart) and quits it after 10
       idle minutes (SIGTERM to this job's own pid); a crash or a quit by hand leaves it down until the next job.
     - deploy/chrome_cross.sh sets the last session aside and execs Chrome with no window and no page
       (no restore-last-session, no start page); its two "backgrounding" switches keep a window behind others, or the
       lock screen, at full speed (WO28).
     - Lower priority than her apps: Nice 10 (Chrome's own QoS-classed threads keep their classes; the nice value lowers
       the rest) and LowPriorityIO (its disk I/O yields to hers). Not ProcessType Background: that clamps every thread to
       background QoS (the efficiency cores, throttled I/O and network) — the throttled, hidden pages of WO28 / WO32b
       stalled live listings inside their 3-minute limit.
     - ExitTimeOut 30: a bootout (the quiet hours, services.sh stop chrome) gives Chrome 30 s to shut down normally. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.thrift.chrome-cross</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>__HOME__/thrift-agent/deploy/chrome_cross.sh</string>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
  <key>Nice</key><integer>10</integer>
  <key>LowPriorityIO</key><true/>
  <key>ExitTimeOut</key><integer>30</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__HOME__/thrift/logs/chrome-cross.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__HOME__/thrift/logs/chrome-cross.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
